        answer: "Pull back grass and examine the layer between green blades and soil. If you see more than 0.5 inches of brown, spongy material, you need dethatching. Test for compaction by trying to push a screwdriver into moist soil - if it won't penetrate easily, you need aeration. Many Treasure Valley lawns need aeration annually but only need dethatching every 3-5 years when thatch genuinely builds up."
